# <type>(<scope>): <subject>

# Mediaway commit template (Conventional Commits 1.0.0) — docs/conventions/commits.md.
# Use: git commit --template=.gitmessage  (the commit-msg hook enforces the shape)
#
# type:  feat | fix | docs | refactor | perf | test | build | ci | chore | revert
# scope: core crate (encoder, container, iso-bmff, ...) | platform crate | backend tech
#        | bindings | binding-<lang> (rust|c|cpp|csharp|python|node|browser)
#        | tools | spec | adr | ci | deps | hooks | docs
# subject: imperative mood, ≤50 chars preferred (72 max), lowercase, no trailing period.
#
# English only — AGENTS.md language policy (commits and PRs are English).
#
# body: why, not what. Streaming/sync-vs-async, Zero-Copy vs copy when it matters.
# footer: BREAKING CHANGE: ... | Refs: #N
